{"id":"word:hebrew:H6010","type":"word","title":"עֵמֶק","subtitle":"H6010 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"a vale (i.e. broad depression)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to עֵמֶק (H6010) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 69 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"עֵמֶק (ʻêmeq) means a vale (i.e. broad depression) First listed occurrence: 1Chr 10 7."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"עֵמֶק","transliteration":"ʻêmeq","pronunciation":"ay'-mek","strong":"H6010","lemmaId":"hebrew:H6010","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["בְּ/עֵ֥מֶק","בְּ/עֵ֖מֶק","עֵ֥מֶק","בָּ/עֵֽמֶק","בְּ/עֵ֣מֶק"],"morphs":[["HR/Ncmsc",22],["HRd/Ncmsa",11],["HNcmsc",10],["HTd/Ncmsa",8],["HC/Ncmsc",5],["HTd/Ncmpa",2],["HRd/Ncmpa",2],["HNcmpa",2],["HNcmpc/Sp2fs",1],["HR/Ncmsa",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"a vale (i.e. broad depression)","usage":"dale, vale, valley (often used as a part of proper names). See also 1025 .","full":"H6010. emeq עֵ֫מֶק 70 noun masculine Micah 1:4 vale (properly deepening, depth , see GASm Geogr. 384 f. 654 f. ; compare נַחַל גַּיְא, בִּקְעָה, ); — ׳י absolute Josh 8:13 +, construct Gen 14:17 +; suffix עִמְקֵךְ Jer 49:4 , עִמְקָם 47:5 (but see below); plural עֲמָקִים Micah 1:4 , suffix עֲמָקַיִךְ Isa 22:7 ; &#8212; vale, valley, lowland , opposed to הֶהָרִים Micah 1:4 , amid mountains, e.g. about Jerusalem Isa 22:7 ; Jer 31:40 , so perhaps ׳ע לשׁוֵה Gen 14:17 = ׳ע הַמֶּלֶךְ 14:17 ; 2Sam 18:18 , compare ׳ע תֶבְרוֺן Gen 37:14 (J), ׳ע בְּגִבְעוֺן Isa 28:21 ; Josh 8:13 (JE), ׳ע הָאֵלָה 1Sam 17:2 , 19 ; 21:10 (perhaps Wady es-Sant , in Shephelah, west of Bethlehem, GASm Geogr. 226 ); ׳ע רְחוֺב לְבֵית אֲשֶׁר Judg 18:28 in extreme north; in Moab Jer 48:8 (|| [opposed to?] מִישׁוֺר ); or wider, e.g. Judg 5:15 (scene of Sisera's defeat; read perhaps ׳ע also for עֲמָלֵק 5:14 GFM), ׳ע יִזְרְעֶ֑אל 6:33 ; Hosea 1:5 ; Josh 17:16 (JE), compare Judg 7:1 , 8 , 12 ; 1Sam 31:7 = 1Chr 10:7 , these all perhaps narrow ends of plain (compare GASm l.c .), but see 1Kin 20:28 (opposed to הֶהָרִים ; || מִישׁוֺר 20:23 ; = open country , compare Aphek 20:26 ); of Jordan-valley Josh 13:19 , 27 (P); of maritime plain (opposed to הָהָר ) Judg 1:19 , 34 ; fit for chariots, so also ׳הָע אֶרֶץ Josh 17:16 (P), compare Job 39:21 ; הָע ׳ישֶׁבֶת Jer 21:13 , compare Num 14:25 (see Gie di); cultivated 1Sam 6:13 ; Jer 49:4 (twice in verse); Job 39:10 , fertile 1Chr 27:29 ; Psalm 65:14; Song 2:1 ; see also כְּרָכָה בָּכָא, אַיָּלוֺן, , II. שִׂדִּים רְפָאִים, קְצִיץ, עָכוֺר, סֻכּוֺת, יְהוֺשָׁפָט, חָרוּץ, ; הָע ׳בֵּית . — For עִמְקָם Jer 47:5 read עֲנָקִם Anakim ᵐ5 Thes Hi Gf Gie Co Rothst; so also (more dubious) 1Chr 12:16 (van d. H. v. 12:15 ) Gf Gie, where otherwise ׳הָע = people of valleys .","rootNote":"from 6009 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 10 7","keyReferences":["1Chr 10 7","1Chr 11 15","1Chr 12 16","1Chr 14 9","1Chr 14 13","1Chr 27 29","1Kgs 20 28","1Sam 6 13"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":69,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 10 7","book":"1Chr","chapter":10,"verse":7,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"בָּ/עֵ֨מֶק֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HRd/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"1Chr 11 15","book":"1Chr","chapter":11,"verse":15,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"בְּ/עֵ֥מֶק","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Ncmsc"},{"reference":"1Chr 12 16","book":"1Chr","chapter":12,"verse":16,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הָ֣/עֲמָקִ֔ים","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncmpa"},{"reference":"1Chr 14 9","book":"1Chr","chapter":14,"verse":9,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"בְּ/עֵ֥מֶק","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Ncmsc"},{"reference":"1Chr 14 13","book":"1Chr","chapter":14,"verse":13,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"בָּ/עֵֽמֶק","source":"hebrew","morph":"HRd/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"1Chr 27 29","book":"1Chr","chapter":27,"verse":29,"englishText":"","sour